I like the idea of Superhero:  No possessions, and great stats & intrinsics.
In fact, you could even get rid of the Aquatic/????? and make an Aquaman.
You could also make a flash with intrinsic speed (*5 if possible).

Realistically, I bet they'd probably be too easy to win with.  If they
find a few usefull items in the first few levels they'd have it made.

What every superhero needs is a good weakness.  If you're going to have
Superman, you need to add Kryptonite as a gem.  It might be kind of
fun to play aquaman -- you'd have to find a pool to lie down in every
1000 moves or so, or else you'd dry up and blow away.  Those yellow
lights would really wreak havoc on a Green Lantern.  (etc.)

Perhaps, a better idea than a superhero is a handicapped character.
People like to brag about having won with every type of character.
We could make one with only one arm (hence only one ring, no two
handed swords or weapons and sheilds), and really low dexterity, etc.

People in other discussions have wanted to change characters like
wizards so they couldn't use weapons -- well why not make an armless
wizard class who COULDN'T wield any weapon.  Or wear any rings.  They
might be able to zap wands.  But basically they's have to win by
casting spells.
